~ start
do Gs._stop()
Narrator: You need go to meeting room
set Gs.event = "meeting"
do Gs._play()
=> END

~ meet
do Gs._stop()
Janitor: Where's the director?
Richard: How should I know?
Deputy director: He went to another city on business.
The guard: That's why we don't have a single penny in our office. I'll run to look for him!*
the methodologist runs away: The director is a bastard! He stole everything and left!
Secretary: You're a brute!  The last scum!  It's not enough to kill!
Manager: No one is allowed to leave the premises! If he comes back, we'll tie him up and hand him over!
Janitor: I'm going to kill this thing with my own hands!
analyst: I'll tear it up on the spot!
Accountant: I won't let you bury him!
Economist: I'll destroy him and scatter his ashes!
Director: * enters from the toilet * Guys, where's the money? Where's the guard? Why are you so angry?
Richard: A security guard? He's gone to look for you...
director: Why are you looking for me? I decided to go to the bathroom on the way ...
* Meanwhile, in the Maldives *
the guard: Well, at least I took a vacation for the first time in 75 years of service.
employee: That's right...
the guard: And where are you from here?
Employee: Got through as luggage.
=> end_meet
=> END

~ end_meet
Narrator: That's the end of the meeting, and the assignment for today is on your screen.
do vis()
do Gs._play()
=> END